---
// Mission: approved 501(c)(3) copy. Reverent typography, generous breathing room.
---

<section id="mission" class="section">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Mission</p>
      <span class="rule mt-6"></span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="reveal mt-10 font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,4rem)] leading-[1.05] text-ink max-w-3xl">
      To uplift lives through the transformative power of music.
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-x-12 gap-y-10">
      <div class="reveal md:col-span-7 space-y-6 text-ink/80 text-[1.05rem] leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Saint John Coltrane Arts is a charitable organization dedicated to providing
          inclusive, high-quality music education and cultural enrichment to underserved
          youth and young adults in San Francisco, particularly in low-income communities.
          Our work is guided by the spiritual and artistic legacy of Saint John Coltrane.
        </p>
        <p>
          We have developed a curriculum-based, multidisciplinary music program that
          integrates music theory, performance, and the science of sound. This program
          fosters creativity, discipline, and community engagement, serving as a vehicle
          for personal growth and academic enrichment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Activities are held weekly at the Saint John Coltrane Church, where participants
          ranging from school-aged youth to young adults engage directly with professional
          musicians and educators. Our team includes university-level instructors and
          PhD-level scholars who mentor students in both individual and ensemble settings.
        </p>
        <p>
          While rooted in musical training, our mission extends beyond music, to promote
          holistic development and access to opportunities that might otherwise be
          unavailable to our students. Through this work, Saint John Coltrane Arts seeks to
          foster a new generation of artists, thinkers, and leaders who carry forward the
          legacy of compassion, excellence, and creative spirit.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="reveal md:col-span-4 md:col-start-9">
        <div class="border-l border-gold/40 pl-6 space-y-8">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow text-muted">Pillars</p>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink/90">
              <li>Theory</li>
              <li>Performance</li>
              <li>The Science of Sound</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow text-muted">Status</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-ink/80">
              501(c)(3) nonprofit. Secular, attached to the Saint John Coltrane Church.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
